  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Investigating Tailwind CSS**\n\nI\'m now diving into how Tailwind CSS is loaded, and I\'m keen to nail down the configuration for our custom elements. The goal is to get those Stitch classes working seamlessly with our custom colors, fonts, and shadows. The aim is for native styling and perfect visual fidelity with all the `bg-surface`, `font-headline-sm`, and `shadow-[...]` classes.\n\n\n**Examining Tailwind Configuration**\n\nI\'m now tracing how the colors, fonts, and sizes are defined in the Stitch project\'s Tailwind config. I\'m focusing on the `@theme` block in v4, as it seems to be the place where custom theming occurs. Specifically, I\'m analyzing the provided JSON configuration to understand how Stitch defines its unique color palette and how that is linked to the Tailwind classes. I\'m hoping to replicate these settings so our elements render faithfully to the original designs.\n\n\n**Analyzing Color and Spacing**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the JSON color definitions, figuring out how Stitch defines its color palette, including things like `on-tertiary-fixed-variant` and `surface-container`.  I\'m also parsing the `spacing` object, mapping the names like \"margin-desktop\" to their values in `rem`. My objective is to completely grasp how these are managed and apply them consistently, in order to get pixel-perfect design. I\'m focusing on the mapping between names and values.\n\n\n**Testing CSS Injection**\n\nNow, I\'m integrating the spacing definitions. I\'m taking the spacing names, like \"gutter-desktop\" and \"space-xl,\" and the accompanying values, and implementing them. My next move is testing them directly in the CSS, by injecting them into `@theme`, to see if the styles apply as planned. I want to see how these map to Tailwind classes. I\'m focusing on the practical application.\n\n\n**Mapping Color Definitions**\n\nI\'m now mapping the specific color definitions, like `--color-primary` to `#ffb4a7` and other variables to their respective hex codes. This process will enable me to apply the appropriate color values from Stitch into our Tailwind configuration, specifically considering how fixed variants like `--color-on-tertiary-fixed-variant` are defined. The goal is to ensure a precise, pixel-perfect match.\n\n\n**Implementing Spacing Variables**\n\nI\'m now integrating the spacing variables, like `--spacing-space-xl`, into the Tailwind configuration. I\'m focusing on directly implementing these variables within the CSS, hoping that the styles will apply as expected. I\'m testing `compile_applet` to see if the custom spacing and font variables compile correctly.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 161521490
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
