  planner_response {
    response: "I have implemented the **BrickForge** web application based on the approved Google Stitch screens and design specifications.\n\n### Visual Identity & Design System\n- **Tactile Brick Aesthetics**: Applied the warm porcelain surface palette (`#fbf8fc`, `#f6f2f7`), deep contrasting text (`#1b1b1e`), rich brick red accents (`#b91000`), and characteristic offset press-down shadows (`shadow-[0_4px_0_0_#910b00]`, `shadow-[0_6px_0_0_#eae7eb]`).\n- **Typography & Iconography**: Integrated Plus Jakarta Sans across all headline and numeric display levels, paired with Google Material Symbols Outlined for technical CAD, assembly, and status indicators.\n- **Responsive Geometry**: Architected fluid layouts supporting both 1440px desktop and 375px mobile viewports with comfortable 48px+ touch targets and adaptive grid structures.\n\n---\n\n### Core Product Flow\n\n1. **Landing View**:\n   - **Hero Transformation**: Displays the input photo alongside the physical ABS brick model render, complete with piece count badges and clutch verification tags.\n   - **Real Builds Showcase**: Features the approved photo-to-brick comparisons (*Golden Retriever*, *Vintage Camera*, *Family Home*) with an interactive model inspector.\n   - **Deliverables Overview**: Highlights the step-by-step PDF assembly guide, complete parts manifest (XML/CSV), and standard LDraw CAD file (`.ldr`).\n   - **Three-Step Blueprint**: Details the workflow from photo upload to physical tabletop assembly.\n\n2. **Upload Photo Flow**:\n   - **Interactive Dropzone**: Supports drag-and-drop file ingestion, local device browsing, and quick selection of approved showcase presets.\n   - **Pre-flight Quality Check**: Validates contrast and contour suitability for 1x1 stud plate resolution.\n\n3. **Photo / Order Preview**:\n   - **Image Inspection**: Features interactive zoom magnification and a quick photo replacement trigger.\n   - **Kit Specifications**: Summarizes piece estimates (~132 pcs), model dimensions (~12 \303\227 10 \303\227 14 cm), builder tier, and color distribution.\n   - **Order Summary**: Outlines the $19.00 USD one-time blueprint package with included digital deliverables and a direct **Build My Model** CTA.\n\n4. **Generation Progress**:\n   - **Assembly Pipeline**: An animated four-stage progress sequence (*Analyzing Photo*, *Synthesizing Brick Structure*, *Checking Clutch & Connections*, *Creating Instructions*).\n   - **Synthesis Sandbox**: Voxel lattice scanline animation displaying real-time stud counts and active layer indicators.\n   - **Craftsmanship Standards**: Rotating technical notes on interlocking seams, commercial ABS tolerances, and LDraw compatibility.\n\n5. **Result & CAD Delivery View**:\n   - **Interactive 3D CAD Viewport**: Features 45\302\260 rotation controls, zoom scaling, view reset, and a toggleable picture-in-picture original photo comparison.\n   - **Assembly Sequence Scrubber**: Allows builders to navigate step-by-step through all 15 stages with sub-assembly titles, descriptions, and piece counters.\n   - **Model Metrics & Palette**: Details total ABS parts, unique mold categories, and a proportional color composition bar.\n   - **Functional File Downloads**: Generates and downloads real `.ldr` LDraw CAD models, `.csv` parts manifests, and printable assembly sheets."
    thinking: "**Verifying Prompt Compliance**\n\nI\'ve confirmed that the applet compilation and linting both succeeded. Now, I\'m meticulously checking the prompt\'s requirements. Currently, I\'m focusing on the product flow, specifically the landing page. I\'m focusing on ensuring the hero section includes a side-by-side photo comparison between a physical MOC and its rendered equivalent, along with calls to action for uploading and learning. Also, there\'s a real build showcase.\n\n\n**Analyzing the Examples**\n\nI\'ve been working on the gallery of approved examples, including the Golden Retriever, Vintage Camera, and Family Home. Each includes a PDF guide, a parts list, and an LDraw 3D CAD file for building. I\'ve broken the starting process down into three steps: Upload, Review, Build. The design emphasizes buildability: actual ABS geometry, standard parts, etc. There\'s a bottom CTA, \"Ready to build something unforgettable?\". I\'m also ensuring the photo upload functionality supports various methods and includes a photo/order preview, responsive for desktop and mobile.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have implemented the **BrickForge** web application based on the approved Google Stitch screens and design specifications.\n\n### Visual Identity & Design System\n- **Tactile Brick Aesthetics**: Applied the warm porcelain surface palette (`#fbf8fc`, `#f6f2f7`), deep contrasting text (`#1b1b1e`), rich brick red accents (`#b91000`), and characteristic offset press-down shadows (`shadow-[0_4px_0_0_#910b00]`, `shadow-[0_6px_0_0_#eae7eb]`).\n- **Typography & Iconography**: Integrated Plus Jakarta Sans across all headline and numeric display levels, paired with Google Material Symbols Outlined for technical CAD, assembly, and status indicators.\n- **Responsive Geometry**: Architected fluid layouts supporting both 1440px desktop and 375px mobile viewports with comfortable 48px+ touch targets and adaptive grid structures.\n\n---\n\n### Core Product Flow\n\n1. **Landing View**:\n   - **Hero Transformation**: Displays the input photo alongside the physical ABS brick model render, complete with piece count badges and clutch verification tags.\n   - **Real Builds Showcase**: Features the approved photo-to-brick comparisons (*Golden Retriever*, *Vintage Camera*, *Family Home*) with an interactive model inspector.\n   - **Deliverables Overview**: Highlights the step-by-step PDF assembly guide, complete parts manifest (XML/CSV), and standard LDraw CAD file (`.ldr`).\n   - **Three-Step Blueprint**: Details the workflow from photo upload to physical tabletop assembly.\n\n2. **Upload Photo Flow**:\n   - **Interactive Dropzone**: Supports drag-and-drop file ingestion, local device browsing, and quick selection of approved showcase presets.\n   - **Pre-flight Quality Check**: Validates contrast and contour suitability for 1x1 stud plate resolution.\n\n3. **Photo / Order Preview**:\n   - **Image Inspection**: Features interactive zoom magnification and a quick photo replacement trigger.\n   - **Kit Specifications**: Summarizes piece estimates (~132 pcs), model dimensions (~12 \303\227 10 \303\227 14 cm), builder tier, and color distribution.\n   - **Order Summary**: Outlines the $19.00 USD one-time blueprint package with included digital deliverables and a direct **Build My Model** CTA.\n\n4. **Generation Progress**:\n   - **Assembly Pipeline**: An animated four-stage progress sequence (*Analyzing Photo*, *Synthesizing Brick Structure*, *Checking Clutch & Connections*, *Creating Instructions*).\n   - **Synthesis Sandbox**: Voxel lattice scanline animation displaying real-time stud counts and active layer indicators.\n   - **Craftsmanship Standards**: Rotating technical notes on interlocking seams, commercial ABS tolerances, and LDraw compatibility.\n\n5. **Result & CAD Delivery View**:\n   - **Interactive 3D CAD Viewport**: Features 45\302\260 rotation controls, zoom scaling, view reset, and a toggleable picture-in-picture original photo comparison.\n   - **Assembly Sequence Scrubber**: Allows builders to navigate step-by-step through all 15 stages with sub-assembly titles, descriptions, and piece counters.\n   - **Model Metrics & Palette**: Details total ABS parts, unique mold categories, and a proportional color composition bar.\n   - **Functional File Downloads**: Generates and downloads real `.ldr` LDraw CAD models, `.csv` parts manifests, and printable assembly sheets."
